            "explanation": {
                "english": "(a) Given reaction is exothermic (ΔH = -ve). Decreasing temperature shifts equilibrium forward, consuming NO₂ (brown), decreasing brown intensity. Correct.\n(b) Increasing pressure shifts equilibrium towards fewer moles of gas (reactants: 2 moles, products: 1 mole), i.e., forward direction, forming more N₂O₄. Correct.\n(c) For an exothermic reaction, equilibrium constant decreases with an increase in temperature according to van 't Hoff equation. Correct.",
